            <title>[LU-21272] o2iblnd: map bulk DMA in IOVA-cacheable chunks</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21272</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Behind a translating IOMMU, every dma_map_sg() allocates one IOVA&lt;br/&gt;
range for the whole scatterlist. The IOMMU layer only caches ranges&lt;br/&gt;
up to dma_opt_mapping_size() (128 KiB on current kernels) per CPU.&lt;br/&gt;
o2iblnd maps a whole LNet bulk (up to 1 MiB, 256 pages) in one call,&lt;br/&gt;
so every bulk map and unmap goes to the rbtree allocator under the&lt;br/&gt;
IOMMU domain's iova_rbtree_lock, first trying the 32-bit window. On&lt;br/&gt;
RoCE clients with the IOMMU in translated mode, Lustre bulk throughput&lt;br/&gt;
drops to 1/2 or 1/3 of line rate on about a third of boots. With&lt;br/&gt;
iommu=pt, 0 of 21 boots degraded, versus 8 of 21 without it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
